      "modify_to": "Localize a resting container by reconstructing its upper horizontal square face on the world z=0.05 m plane. Identify that face's four outer corners, excluding vertical side faces and the lower rim; do not use the whole silhouette or the grasp TCP height as the reconstruction plane. For each corner pixel p=(u,v,1), compute the camera center C=-R^T t and world ray d=R^T K^{-1}p using the view's calibration. Intersect the ray with the face plane: X=C+((0.05-C_z)/d_z)d. Average the four reconstructed corners to obtain the grasp-axis x,y, and recover yaw from the reconstructed square edges. If corners are obscured, fit the square to visible top-face edges and check against the other calibrated view rather than averaging the silhouette. Use the current wrist-camera extrinsics for the wrist view. Command the open-hand approach at this reconstructed x,y and z=0.20 m."
    },
    {
      "modify_from": "Use visible geometry to correct lateral approach error without inserting an extra approach waypoint.",
      "modify_to": "At approach height, reconstruct the same top face again using the current calibrated wrist image, checked against the front view, to correct lateral undershoot. Descend directly to the reconstructed x,y at the grasp TCP height and close, without inserting an extra approach waypoint. The z=0.05 m reconstruction plane is distinct from the z=0.0633 m grasp TCP height."
    }
  ],
  "refused": "The proposed change of grasp TCP height from 0.0633 m to 0.0634 m is not committed: the reported failure concerns lateral localization, and this 0.1 mm change does not address it. Memory and the existing target-association, lift, replacement, and clearance rules remain unchanged."
